    "description": "Custom milestone day 1 description"
  },
  "customMilestone3Title": "Withdrawal Symptoms Peak",
  "@customMilestone3Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 3 title"
  },
  "customMilestone3Description": "You're facing the storm head-on! Physical withdrawal symptoms typically peak around day 3 for many substances, including anxiety, mood swings, and physical discomfort. This means you're getting through the hardest part.",
  "@customMilestone3Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 3 description"
  },
  "customMilestone7Title": "Acute Withdrawal Phase Ending",
  "@customMilestone7Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 7 title"
  },
  "customMilestone7Description": "The worst is behind you! After one week, acute withdrawal symptoms begin to subside for most substances. Your body is adjusting to its new normal and starting to stabilize.",
  "@customMilestone7Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 7 description"
  },
  "customMilestone14Title": "Early Recovery Stabilization",
  "@customMilestone14Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 14 title"
  },
  "customMilestone14Description": "Your mind is clearing! Two weeks of sobriety often brings improved mental clarity and reduced cravings as your brain begins to adapt to functioning without addictive substances.",
  "@customMilestone14Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 14 description"
  },
  "customMilestone30Title": "One Month Milestone",
  "@customMilestone30Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 30 title"
  },
  "customMilestone30Description": "A major victory! Thirty days of sobriety represents significant progress. Many people find that sleep patterns, mood, and energy levels continue to improve during this period.",
  "@customMilestone30Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 30 description"
  },
  "customMilestone90Title": "Three Month Recovery Milestone",
  "@customMilestone90Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 90 title"
  },
  "customMilestone90Description": "Your commitment is paying off! Three months of recovery represents a significant achievement. Post-acute withdrawal symptoms typically begin to fade, and many people report feeling more like themselves again.",
  "@customMilestone90Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 90 description"
  },
  "customMilestone180Title": "Six Month Recovery Achievement",
  "@customMilestone180Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 180 title"
  },
  "customMilestone180Description": "You're building lasting change! Six months of sobriety often brings continued improvements in physical health, emotional stability, and overall quality of life as your body continues healing.",
  "@customMilestone180Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 180 description"
  },
  "customMilestone365Title": "One Year of Recovery",
  "@customMilestone365Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 365 title"
  },
  "customMilestone365Description": "An incredible achievement! One year of sobriety represents a major life milestone. Many people experience significant improvements in physical health, relationships, and overall well-being by this point.",
  "@customMilestone365Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 365 description"
  },
  "customMilestone730Title": "Two Years of Sustained Recovery",
  "@customMilestone730Title": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 730 title"
  },
  "customMilestone730Description": "You've built a new life! Two years of recovery demonstrates remarkable resilience and commitment. Long-term sobriety often brings profound positive changes in all areas of life and significantly reduced risk of relapse.",
  "@customMilestone730Description": {
    "description": "Custom milestone day 730 description"
  },
